UMBRA Brain v0+v1: provider abstraction, gateway, doctor, privacy router

The Brain router era - one gateway, many models, privacy-first routing.

v0 - provider abstraction + gateway + doctor:
- brain/ package: the legacy brain.py content is preserved verbatim as
  brain/__init__.py (every existing import keeps working) and the new
  layers live in submodules. providers/base.py defines the Provider
  interface (chat, stream, tools, vision, embed, health);
  providers/ollama.py adapts Ollama's native /api surface with an
  injectable transport (tests mock HTTP, no network);
  providers/openai_compat.py composes the proven legacy Brain.
- manifest.py: per-model capability manifests (id, locality, tools,
  vision, context, costs, latency, strengths, privacy_class) with schema
  validation; built-ins for the default local brain; user manifests
  override built-ins by id from <config>/manifests/*.json.
- complete(request): the single gateway - behavior-preserving, drives the
  same BrainChain machinery and records the route (model, failover) as
  metadata. classify_error() adds timeout/auth/rate-limit/server/
  connection classes for fallback decisions.
- jarvis doctor: Python, config, license, local-brain reachability +
  model presence, update-check reachability, EDITH ledger integrity -
  each with a fix hint. Always exit 0 (a report, not a gate).

v1 - the privacy router:
- router.py pipeline: sensitivity check (paths, emails, key shapes,
  screen-content markers) -> task classification (keyword rules) ->
  candidate filter (capabilities + context) -> budget filter (per-request
  and daily caps) -> selection (strength match, then cheapest,
  local-first on ties) -> privacy-preserving fallback order.
- Cloud providers are opt-in per provider (config router.cloud_providers);
  sensitive text NEVER routes to a cloud model (tested); the redaction
  gate scrubs paths/emails/keys/license shapes before any cloud call.
- Route log (route-log.jsonl): model id, intent, sensitivity, cost and
  latency estimates - never the prompt text. jarvis brain status and
  jarvis brain route --explain "<prompt>" (dry run, no network).
- config: additive RouterConfig section (cloud_providers,
  max_cost_per_request, daily_budget); settings show/set cover the
  budgets.
- Tests: provider contract against the mock and the Ollama adapter with
  mocked HTTP; manifest validation; gateway failover; doctor report;
  classification; sensitivity pinning; vision-capability filtering;
  budget enforcement; redaction; route-log privacy.
- Version 3.21.0 (v0 and v1 ship together; versions bump per mark, not
  per sub-phase).
